1
00:00:00,900 --> 00:00:02,550
This is CatatMD.

2
00:00:02,600 --> 00:00:07,510
It turns a GP consultation into a clinical
note the doctor can review.

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:12,128
Everything you'll see here is synthetic:
no real patient appears.

4
00:00:14,600 --> 00:00:19,081
The doctor registers a patient and starts
a consultation from the profile.

5
00:00:23,200 --> 00:00:26,368
With the patient's consent, given for this
visit only,

6
00:00:26,418 --> 00:00:28,963
the doctor records the consultation.

7
00:00:31,700 --> 00:00:37,600
Patient: …this morning there were a few
streaks of blood in my phlegm.

8
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:41,987
When the doctor stops, a speech service in
Malaysia transcribes it.

9
00:00:45,900 --> 00:00:48,099
One click analyses the visit.

10
00:00:49,900 --> 00:00:55,066
Before any text leaves the server, names
and identity numbers become tokens.

11
00:00:55,200 --> 00:00:57,310
The model only ever sees the tokens,

12
00:00:57,360 --> 00:01:00,761
and the real details come back on the
return trip.

13
00:01:05,900 --> 00:01:08,496
The doctor reviews three panels side by
side:

14
00:01:08,546 --> 00:01:12,050
the transcript, the structured note, and
clinical safety.

15
00:01:12,100 --> 00:01:15,150
Red flags come from deterministic rules
first.

16
00:01:15,200 --> 00:01:20,034
The model can add candidates for review,
but it can never remove a rule's hit.

17
00:01:27,100 --> 00:01:30,551
The checklist ties each field to the words
that support it.

18
00:01:32,500 --> 00:01:35,572
Suggestions cite guideline IDs from a
fixed corpus,

19
00:01:35,622 --> 00:01:38,900
so a made-up reference cannot reach the
screen.

20
00:01:40,600 --> 00:01:43,573
The doctor writes the prescription in
plain words.

21
00:01:46,400 --> 00:01:50,698
CatatMD parses each line into dose,
frequency and duration,

22
00:01:50,748 --> 00:01:54,465
and saves only the lines the doctor
confirms.

23
00:01:57,300 --> 00:01:59,650
Nothing is ever approved by default.

24
00:01:59,700 --> 00:02:03,479
The doctor acknowledges the red flags and
approves the note.

25
00:02:11,100 --> 00:02:14,683
The finished record exports as a
consultation report.

26
00:02:19,500 --> 00:02:21,050
CatatMD drafts.

27
00:02:21,100 --> 00:02:22,749
The doctor decides.
